822 0 obj
<</Title(Depending on your arrival time, your first encounter with this extraordinary country begins in Sidi Bou Said \204 a spellbinding artist's village perched above the Gulf of Tunis, its cobalt-blue shutters and immaculate whitewashed walls tumbling down limestone hillsides above a shimmering sea. Poets and painters have been captivated here for generations.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 756 0 R/Prev 810 0 R/Next 823 0 R>>
endobj

823 0 obj
<</Title(The afternoon continues with a private visit to the Erlanger Palace, a masterwork of Moorish-Andalusian architecture whose tiled salons and perfumed gardens reveal the opulent world of Tunisia's Bey era.)/Dest[13 0 R/Fit]/Parent 756 0 R/Prev 822 0 R/Next 811 0 R>>
endobj

824 0 obj
<</Title(DAY 02  \267  TUNIS)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 811 0 R>>
endobj

825 0 obj
<</Title(Step into the labyrinthine heart of medieval Tunis \204 the Medina, a UNESCO World Heritage Site since 1979. Wander beneath vaulted arches to the Zitouna Mosque \(exterior\), the exquisite beylical house Dar Lasram, and the legendary souks organised by craft: perfumers, jewellers, leather artisans, weavers \204 each lane a living museum of Tunisian savoir-faire.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 812 0 R/Next 834 0 R>>
endobj

826 0 obj
<</Title(Dinner and overnight in Tunis.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 812 0 R/Prev 834 0 R/First 835 0 R/Last 835 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

827 0 obj
<</Title(ANCIENT PORTS & WILD NORTHERN COAST)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 812 0 R/First 836 0 R/Last 837 0 R/Count -3/Next 838 0 R>>
endobj

828 0 obj
<</Title(EL JEM \267 MONASTIR \267 SOUSSE \267 HAMMAMET)/Dest[23 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 839 0 R/First 840 0 R/Last 841 0 R/Count -3/Next 813 0 R>>
endobj

829 0 obj
<</Title(A gentle morning devoted to Hammamet's enchanting Medina \204 one of the smallest and most perfectly proportioned in Tunisia, its pristine whitewashed ramparts rising directly from the turquoise Mediterranean. Walk its jasmine-scented alleys and enter the Kasbah, a compact 15th-century fortress offering sweeping panoramas over the curved bay and the endless glittering sea beyond.)/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 813 0 R/Next 842 0 R>>
endobj

830 0 obj
<</Title(Lunch, dinner and overnight in Hammamet.)/Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 813 0 R/Prev 842 0 R/First 843 0 R/Last 843 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

831 0 obj
<</Title(Then Carthage \204 once mistress of the Mediterranean, rival of Rome, queen of ancient seas. Walk among the Tanit Sanctuary and the atmospheric Punic ports. Climb Byrsa Hill for its panoramic view across the Gulf of Tunis, then descend to the breathtaking Antonine Baths \204 among the largest thermal complexes ever built in the Roman world, their columns still standing proud against an impossibly blue Carthaginian sky.)/Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 757 0 R/Prev 814 0 R/Next 815 0 R>>
endobj

832 0 obj
<</Title(Bulla Regia  \267  Dougga  \267  Kairouan)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 702 0 R/Prev 820 0 R/Next 844 0 R>>
endobj

