<</Title(El Jem Amphitheatre  \267  Monastir  \267  Sousse  \267  Hammamet)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 702 0 R/Prev 845 0 R/Next 821 0 R>>
endobj

834 0 obj
<</Title(Lunch at a heritage-listed restaurant within the medina walls, then an afternoon at the Bardo Museum: a 19th-century beylical palace housing one of the world's finest collections of Roman mosaics. An afternoon that redefines magnificence.)/Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 812 0 R/Prev 825 0 R/Next 826 0 R>>
endobj

835 0 obj
<</Title(DAY 03  \267  UTICA \267 TABARKA)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 826 0 R>>
endobj

836 0 obj
<</Title(Depart for Utica \204 one of the oldest Phoenician settlements on African soil and once the proud capital of the Roman province of Africa Vetus. Explore the archaeological site: the Punic necropolis, the beautifully preserved Roman houses and the haunting quiet of a city that outlived its empire.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 827 0 R/Next 846 0 R>>
endobj

837 0 obj
<</Title(Dinner and overnight in Tabarka.)/Dest[15 0 R/Fit]/Parent 827 0 R/Prev 846 0 R/First 847 0 R/Last 847 0 R/Count -1>>
