endobj

866 0 obj
<</Title(Journey into the ancient world of the Berbers. Matmata presents one of Tunisia's most surreal vistas: a community of troglodyte dwellings carved directly into the earth \204 circular open courtyards surrounded by cave-like chambers, some inhabited across countless generations. Visit and lunch.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 851 0 R/Next 879 0 R>>
endobj

867 0 obj
<</Title(Dinner and overnight in Tataouine.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 851 0 R/Prev 879 0 R/First 880 0 R/Last 880 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

868 0 obj
<</Title(Visit the haunting abandoned Berber village of Douiret: pale stone houses terraced up a hillside beneath a crumbling ksar, achingly beautiful in its stillness \204 a world paused, not destroyed.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 839 0 R/Prev 852 0 R/Next 869 0 R>>
endobj

869 0 obj
<</Title(Lunch before heading north to Sfax, Tunisia's industrious second city, celebrated for its magnificent walled medina and centuries of maritime and mercantile tradition.)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 839 0 R/Prev 868 0 R/Next 853 0 R>>
endobj

870 0 obj
<</Title(Chebika  \267  Tamerza  \267  Mides Canyon  \267  Tozeur Palm Grove)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 702 0 R/Prev 857 0 R/Next 871 0 R>>
