871 0 obj
<</Title(Dar Chraiet  \267  Chott El Jerid  \267  Douz  \267  Sahara)/Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 702 0 R/Prev 870 0 R/Next 858 0 R>>
endobj

872 0 obj
<</Title(Visit the Grande Mosque, founded in 670 AD, considered the oldest in the Maghreb. Its forest of Roman and Byzantine columns, ancient prayer hall and iconic ribbed dome inspire profound contemplation across fourteen centuries. Continue to the Barbier Mosque and marvel at the Aghlabide Basins \204 magnificent 9th-century hydraulic engineering. The afternoon unfolds through the medina's intricate alleys, past craftsmen weaving celebrated Kairouan carpets and merchants of hand-crafted brassware and sweet makroudh pastries.)/Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Parent 850 0 R/Prev 862 0 R/Next 863 0 R>>
endobj

873 0 obj
<</Title(DAY 06  \267  KAIROUAN \211 SBEITLA\211 TOZEUR)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 863 0 R>>
endobj

874 0 obj
<</Title(Journey across the high steppe to Sbeitla \204 ancient Sufetula \204 where three remarkably intact Roman temples rise side by side on a monumental forum beneath an immense sky. One of Tunisia's most dramatic archaeological tableaux, and one of its most quietly moving.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 864 0 R/Next 881 0 R>>
endobj

875 0 obj
<</Title(Dinner and overnight in Tozeur.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 864 0 R/Prev 881 0 R/First 882 0 R/Last 882 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

876 0 obj
<</Title(CHEBIKA \267 TAMERZA \267 MIDES CANYON)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 864 0 R/First 883 0 R/Last 884 0 R/Count -3/Next 865 0 R>>
endobj

877 0 obj
<</Title(The morning opens at the Dar Chraiet Museum, an opulent private collection celebrating the finest of Tunisian decorative heritage. Then begins an otherworldly crossing of Chott El Jerid \204 an immense salt lake stretching to every horizon, where shimmering mirages conjure phantom lakes and inverted cities in the heat-hazed distance. A landscape unlike anything else on Earth.)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 865 0 R/Next 885 0 R>>
endobj

878 0 obj
<</Title(Lunch, dinner and overnight in Douz.)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 865 0 R/Prev 885 0 R/First 886 0 R/Last 886 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

879 0 obj
<</Title(Continue further south into the Ksours region, a landscape of otherworldly beauty. The perched Berber village of Chenini ranks among the most dramatically sited human settlements imaginable \204 its ruined mosque and pale stone houses clinging to a rocky spur above the desert plain, shimmering in the late afternoon light.)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 851 0 R/Prev 866 0 R/Next 867 0 R>>
endobj

880 0 obj
<</Title(DAY 10  \267  TATAOUINE \211 SFAX)/Dest[22 0 R/Fit]/Parent 867 0 R>>
endobj

881 0 obj
<</Title(Lunch before heading south as the landscape transforms dramatically: terracotta earth gives way to the golden palmeraie as you approach Tozeur, the enchanting oasis city at the edge of the Sahara. Tozeur enchants with its extraordinary brickwork architecture \204 an ancient decorative tradition unique to this region, each facade a geometric arabesque in warm honey-coloured stone.)/Dest[18 0 R/Fit]/Parent 864 0 R/Prev 874 0 R/Next 875 0 R>>
endobj

882 0 obj
<</Title(DAY 07  \267  TOZEUR)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 875 0 R>>
endobj

883 0 obj
<</Title(Embark on a cinematic half-day 4\3274 expedition through the mountain oases of Chebika, Tamerza and Mides \204 once Roman frontier outposts, today among Tunisia's most ethereal landscapes. Waterfalls cascade through golden gorges, abandoned Berber villages cling to cliffsides, and the canyon of Mides carves a breathtaking passage through ancient sandstone, its silence broken only by the sound of running water.)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 876 0 R/Next 887 0 R>>
endobj

884 0 obj
<</Title(Dinner and overnight in Tozeur.)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 876 0 R/Prev 887 0 R/First 888 0 R/Last 888 0 R/Count -1>>
endobj

885 0 obj
<</Title(Arrival at Douz, Gateway to the Sahara. A camel ride towards the village of Zaafrane \204 at the very edge of the Grand Erg Oriental \204 offers an encounter with the great golden silence of the Sahara that will remain with you always.)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 865 0 R/Prev 877 0 R/Next 878 0 R>>
endobj

886 0 obj
<</Title(DAY 09  \267  DOUZ \211MATMATA\211 TATAOUINE)/Dest[21 0 R/Fit]/Parent 878 0 R>>
endobj

887 0 obj
<</Title(Return to Tozeur for lunch and exploration of the medina's arcaded streets. As the afternoon light turns amber, a carriage ride through the magnificent palm grove \204 home to some 400,000 date palms \204 offers a moment of pure poetry, completed with a visit to the exhibition centre dedicated to the legendary Deglet Nour date.)/Dest[19 0 R/Fit]/Parent 876 0 R/Prev 883 0 R/Next 884 0 R>>
endobj

888 0 obj
<</Title(DAY 08  \267  TOZEUR \211CHOTT JERID\211 DOUZ)/Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 884 0 R>>
